            "created_at": "2025-09-11T22:37:23.537084+00:00",
            "notes": "If you make it here, you probably already won, because [Signature Shift](item_665f2250-6c78-439a-8ea8-6d5c8124e73c) works so well with this build it should be a crime. Enjoy your screenshot with 15k+ damage dealt in one round.\n\nAt this point, weapon power becomes a lot more appealing than before, so there are several routes we can take with this build. \n\n [Sonic Recharger](item_c5e6a2c9-1bed-48fa-b539-01e76098a297) is 100 more HP. The overhealth restoration rate depends on our max HP. This item is crucial to dealing with hitscan characters that went weapon power. If we don't have enough HP, then we won't even be able to get close to them without dying. \n\n [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) is for when we've decided Rein or Orisa or Dva needed to die. That happens quite a bit, believe it or not. At this stage, we melt tanks, and sometimes tanks are the only characters on the enemy team that can't use an ability to escape our burst comboes, in which case we go after them. They also have a harder time seeing us coming, because they have to deal with a lot more pressure in general.\n\n [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b) combined with  [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) is 40% weapon damage for 20000 cash, which is the best rate for weapon damage. If we have the income, and we don't need the extra health from sonic recharger, it will give us the best shot at melting people. \n\n [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) is a happy middle between damage and survivability. If we have enough cash, we should definitely take this over talon modification module. \n\nI'm also considering [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448), because cooldown reduction is very good in this build, it allows us to combo people more often.",
